# Copy to admin/.env — never commit the real file.
#
# Both values below are PUBLIC by design (bundled into the admin app's
# JS, same as any Vite VITE_-prefixed variable). That's expected and
# safe here: the anon key identifies "a client of this Supabase
# project," nothing more. Row Level Security — not this key — is what
# actually decides whether a signed-in user can read anything. See
# ../ADMIN-DASHBOARD-ARCHITECTURE.md and src/lib/supabaseClient.js for
# the full reasoning.
#
# The SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY that bypasses RLS entirely must NEVER
# go in this file, or in any VITE_-prefixed variable anywhere. It only
# ever belongs in backend/.env and in the shell environment you run
# database/scripts/create-admin-user.mjs from.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
